  "question": {
    "text": "Two fair dice, each with faces numbered&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>, are rolled together and the sum of the numbers on the faces is observed. This process is repeated till the sum is either a prime number or a perfect square. Suppose the sum turns out to be a perfect square before it turns out to be a prime number. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is the probability that this perfect square is an odd number, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mi>p</mi></math> is_____"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Perfect Square can be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>,&nbsp;which can be obtained by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Prime Number can be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math>, which can be obtained by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>(square or prime)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mtext>&#160;Perfect square&#160;is&#160;odd&#160;</mtext><mtext>&#160;perfect square&#160;before prime&#160;</mtext></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>.</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>.</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>.</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>.</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>.</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>.</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p>"
  }
